	data5.put("Section 1 Question 8", "What should I do if an unexpected error message, warning, validation message, loading indicator, or technical problem prevents me from completing an action involving search engine visibility and patient portal accessibility?");
	data5.put("Section 1 Answer 8", "Read the complete error or warning and review required fields, statuses, and instructions before trying again. If the issue appears technical, note the page, action performed, message, device, browser, and approximate time. Avoid repeated submissions when the action could create duplicate healthcare, payment, appointment, treatment, or ordering records, and contact support if the problem persists. This guidance applies specifically to search engine visibility and patient portal accessibility and is intentionally lengthy so the frontend can be checked for multi-line wrapping, accordion expansion, spacing, clipping, overlap, and responsive behavior.");
	data5.put("Section 1 Question 9", "What information should I review and prepare before contacting patient support or the healthcare team about a problem involving search engine visibility and patient portal accessibility so the issue can be investigated without unnecessary repeated actions?");
	data5.put("Section 1 Answer 9", "Review the affected record, current status, relevant dates, recent notifications, exact action attempted, and any error or confirmation message. Be ready to explain the expected and actual result. Do not share passwords, active verification codes, complete payment credentials, or other authentication secrets. Clear context helps authorized support investigate the issue without unnecessary repeated steps. This guidance applies specifically to search engine visibility and patient portal accessibility and is intentionally lengthy so the frontend can be checked for multi-line wrapping, accordion expansion, spacing, clipping, overlap, and responsive behavior.");
	data5.put("Section 1 Question 10", "How can I tell whether a problem involving search engine visibility and patient portal accessibility is a temporary portal display issue, an expected healthcare workflow condition, or something that requires support or clinical assistance before I continue?");
	data5.put("Section 1 Answer 10", "Refresh or reopen the relevant area when appropriate and check whether the latest information has synchronized. Then review any displayed status, required next step, restriction, or notification that could explain the behavior. If the issue could affect a clinical, financial, scheduling, prescription, laboratory, or fulfillment decision, obtain clarification before continuing. This guidance applies specifically to search engine visibility and patient portal accessibility and is intentionally lengthy so the frontend can be checked for multi-line wrapping, accordion expansion, spacing, clipping, overlap, and responsive behavior.");
	data5.put("Section 1 Question 11", "Who should I contact when every normal self-service option and reasonable troubleshooting step related to search engine visibility and patient portal accessibility has already been attempted but the problem still prevents me from completing the intended healthcare activity?");
	data5.put("Section 1 Answer 11", "Use the authorized support channel for the affected workflow. Technical problems involving page behavior, missing controls, errors, or account access can be reported to patient portal support, while medication, symptom, treatment, or other clinical questions should be directed to an appropriately authorized healthcare professional. Serious emergencies should never wait for routine portal support. This guidance applies specifically to search engine visibility and patient portal accessibility and is intentionally lengthy so the frontend can be checked for multi-line wrapping, accordion expansion, spacing, clipping, overlap, and responsive behavior.");

