	data5.put("Section 2 Question Count", "11");
	data5.put("Section 2 Question 1", "What should I do if the information, status, control, or expected action related to portal availability status and redirection assistance does not appear correctly in the patient portal even after I carefully review the page and wait for normal processing to finish?");
	data5.put("Section 2 Answer 1", "Review the complete information shown in the relevant portal area and confirm that you are using the correct patient record, treatment, appointment, prescription, order, laboratory activity, or account information. Allow normal processing time and verify that no required step was missed. If the expected information remains unavailable, avoid repeated submissions and contact authorized support. This guidance applies specifically to portal availability status and redirection assistance and is intentionally lengthy so the frontend can be checked for multi-line wrapping, accordion expansion, spacing, clipping, overlap, and responsive behavior.");
	data5.put("Section 2 Question 2", "Why might the details shown for portal availability status and redirection assistance become different from information I previously viewed in the portal, received through a notification, or discussed with the healthcare organization during an earlier interaction?");
	data5.put("Section 2 Answer 2", "The displayed information can change after updates from providers, administrators, pharmacies, laboratories, payment systems, fulfillment services, or other connected workflows. Compare the latest portal status with recent notifications or messages. If the difference could affect treatment, payment, scheduling, delivery, or another important decision, contact the appropriate healthcare team before proceeding. This guidance applies specifically to portal availability status and redirection assistance and is intentionally lengthy so the frontend can be checked for multi-line wrapping, accordion expansion, spacing, clipping, overlap, and responsive behavior.");
	data5.put("Section 2 Question 3", "How can I confirm that an important action involving portal availability status and redirection assistance was actually submitted and saved successfully when the page changes slowly or the final confirmation message is not immediately visible?");
	data5.put("Section 2 Answer 3", "Look for a success message, updated status, newly created record, changed value, or another visible confirmation. If the final result is unclear, review the associated history before trying again because the original request may already have succeeded. Repeating the action without checking can create duplicate orders, appointments, payments, refill requests, or other records. This guidance applies specifically to portal availability status and redirection assistance and is intentionally lengthy so the frontend can be checked for multi-line wrapping, accordion expansion, spacing, clipping, overlap, and responsive behavior.");
	data5.put("Section 2 Question 4", "What should I verify before repeating an action related to portal availability status and redirection assistance when the patient portal appears slow, partially loaded, temporarily unresponsive, or unable to display the expected result?");
	data5.put("Section 2 Answer 4", "Before repeating the action, confirm that the first attempt did not already create the expected result. Review the latest status, history, confirmation messages, and related patient information. Refresh only when appropriate and allow normal processing time. If the outcome remains uncertain, contact support instead of repeatedly clicking a control while the application may still be processing. This guidance applies specifically to portal availability status and redirection assistance and is intentionally lengthy so the frontend can be checked for multi-line wrapping, accordion expansion, spacing, clipping, overlap, and responsive behavior.");
	data5.put("Section 2 Question 5", "What should I do if information connected with portal availability status and redirection assistance appears incomplete, duplicated, outdated, inconsistent, or unexpectedly different from what I believe should currently be associated with my patient account?");
	data5.put("Section 2 Answer 5", "Compare identifiers, dates, statuses, treatment or product details, provider information, payment amounts, order information, and other visible context. Do not assume that duplicated or inconsistent records are harmless. If the difference cannot be explained from the portal, contact the healthcare organization so an authorized user can determine whether the data is current, historical, intentionally separate, or incorrect. This guidance applies specifically to portal availability status and redirection assistance and is intentionally lengthy so the frontend can be checked for multi-line wrapping, accordion expansion, spacing, clipping, overlap, and responsive behavior.");
	data5.put("Section 2 Question 6", "Why might a feature, button, field, status, or other option related to portal availability status and redirection assistance be available in one situation but unavailable in another even though I can still access the patient portal normally?");
