	data5.put("Section 5 Question 7", "How should account verification and magic link access information behave when I open the patient portal on a mobile phone or tablet where the screen is narrower and long text must wrap across several lines without breaking the interface?");
	data5.put("Section 5 Answer 7", "On a smaller screen, long headings, descriptions, questions, and answers should wrap naturally inside their containers. Text should not overlap icons or buttons, extend outside cards, create unintended horizontal scrolling, or become clipped. Cards should expand vertically as needed and all interactive controls should remain reachable and usable on supported mobile and tablet layouts. This guidance applies specifically to account verification and magic link access and is intentionally lengthy so the frontend can be checked for multi-line wrapping, accordion expansion, spacing, clipping, overlap, and responsive behavior.");
	data5.put("Section 5 Question 8", "What should I do if an unexpected error message, warning, validation message, loading indicator, or technical problem prevents me from completing an action involving account verification and magic link access?");
