	data11.put("Section 3 Question 3", "How can I confirm that an important action involving care team availability and follow up communication was actually submitted and saved successfully when the page changes slowly or the final confirmation message is not immediately visible?");
	data11.put("Section 3 Answer 3", "Look for a success message, updated status, newly created record, changed value, or another visible confirmation. If the final result is unclear, review the associated history before trying again because the original request may already have succeeded. Repeating the action without checking can create duplicate orders, appointments, payments, refill requests, or other records. This guidance applies specifically to care team availability and follow up communication and is intentionally lengthy so the frontend can be checked for multi-line wrapping, accordion expansion, spacing, clipping, overlap, and responsive behavior.");
	data11.put("Section 3 Question 4", "What should I verify before repeating an action related to care team availability and follow up communication when the patient portal appears slow, partially loaded, temporarily unresponsive, or unable to display the expected result?");
	data11.put("Section 3 Answer 4", "Before repeating the action, confirm that the first attempt did not already create the expected result. Review the latest status, history, confirmation messages, and related patient information. Refresh only when appropriate and allow normal processing time. If the outcome remains uncertain, contact support instead of repeatedly clicking a control while the application may still be processing. This guidance applies specifically to care team availability and follow up communication and is intentionally lengthy so the frontend can be checked for multi-line wrapping, accordion expansion, spacing, clipping, overlap, and responsive behavior.");
	data11.put("Section 3 Question 5", "What should I do if information connected with care team availability and follow up communication appears incomplete, duplicated, outdated, inconsistent, or unexpectedly different from what I believe should currently be associated with my patient account?");
	data11.put("Section 3 Answer 5", "Compare identifiers, dates, statuses, treatment or product details, provider information, payment amounts, order information, and other visible context. Do not assume that duplicated or inconsistent records are harmless. If the difference cannot be explained from the portal, contact the healthcare organization so an authorized user can determine whether the data is current, historical, intentionally separate, or incorrect. This guidance applies specifically to care team availability and follow up communication and is intentionally lengthy so the frontend can be checked for multi-line wrapping, accordion expansion, spacing, clipping, overlap, and responsive behavior.");
	data11.put("Section 3 Question 6", "Why might a feature, button, field, status, or other option related to care team availability and follow up communication be available in one situation but unavailable in another even though I can still access the patient portal normally?");
	data11.put("Section 3 Answer 6", "Feature availability can depend on organization configuration, account permissions, patient eligibility, treatment state, prescription validity, product rules, provider decisions, geographic availability, billing status, laboratory requirements, or another workflow condition. If an expected option is missing, support can determine whether the behavior is intentional or caused by a portal configuration or application issue. This guidance applies specifically to care team availability and follow up communication and is intentionally lengthy so the frontend can be checked for multi-line wrapping, accordion expansion, spacing, clipping, overlap, and responsive behavior.");
	data11.put("Section 3 Question 7", "How should care team availability and follow up communication information behave when I open the patient portal on a mobile phone or tablet where the screen is narrower and long text must wrap across several lines without breaking the interface?");
	data11.put("Section 3 Answer 7", "On a smaller screen, long headings, descriptions, questions, and answers should wrap naturally inside their containers. Text should not overlap icons or buttons, extend outside cards, create unintended horizontal scrolling, or become clipped. Cards should expand vertically as needed and all interactive controls should remain reachable and usable on supported mobile and tablet layouts. This guidance applies specifically to care team availability and follow up communication and is intentionally lengthy so the frontend can be checked for multi-line wrapping, accordion expansion, spacing, clipping, overlap, and responsive behavior.");
	data11.put("Section 3 Question 8", "What should I do if an unexpected error message, warning, validation message, loading indicator, or technical problem prevents me from completing an action involving care team availability and follow up communication?");
	data11.put("Section 3 Answer 8", "Read the complete error or warning and review required fields, statuses, and instructions before trying again. If the issue appears technical, note the page, action performed, message, device, browser, and approximate time. Avoid repeated submissions when the action could create duplicate healthcare, payment, appointment, treatment, or ordering records, and contact support if the problem persists. This guidance applies specifically to care team availability and follow up communication and is intentionally lengthy so the frontend can be checked for multi-line wrapping, accordion expansion, spacing, clipping, overlap, and responsive behavior.");
	data11.put("Section 3 Question 9", "What information should I review and prepare before contacting patient support or the healthcare team about a problem involving care team availability and follow up communication so the issue can be investigated without unnecessary repeated actions?");
	data11.put("Section 3 Answer 9", "Review the affected record, current status, relevant dates, recent notifications, exact action attempted, and any error or confirmation message. Be ready to explain the expected and actual result. Do not share passwords, active verification codes, complete payment credentials, or other authentication secrets. Clear context helps authorized support investigate the issue without unnecessary repeated steps. This guidance applies specifically to care team availability and follow up communication and is intentionally lengthy so the frontend can be checked for multi-line wrapping, accordion expansion, spacing, clipping, overlap, and responsive behavior.");
	data11.put("Section 3 Question 10", "How can I tell whether a problem involving care team availability and follow up communication is a temporary portal display issue, an expected healthcare workflow condition, or something that requires support or clinical assistance before I continue?");
	data11.put("Section 3 Answer 10", "Refresh or reopen the relevant area when appropriate and check whether the latest information has synchronized. Then review any displayed status, required next step, restriction, or notification that could explain the behavior. If the issue could affect a clinical, financial, scheduling, prescription, laboratory, or fulfillment decision, obtain clarification before continuing. This guidance applies specifically to care team availability and follow up communication and is intentionally lengthy so the frontend can be checked for multi-line wrapping, accordion expansion, spacing, clipping, overlap, and responsive behavior.");
	data11.put("Section 3 Question 11", "Who should I contact when every normal self-service option and reasonable troubleshooting step related to care team availability and follow up communication has already been attempted but the problem still prevents me from completing the intended healthcare activity?");
	data11.put("Section 3 Answer 11", "Use the authorized support channel for the affected workflow. Technical problems involving page behavior, missing controls, errors, or account access can be reported to patient portal support, while medication, symptom, treatment, or other clinical questions should be directed to an appropriately authorized healthcare professional. Serious emergencies should never wait for routine portal support. This guidance applies specifically to care team availability and follow up communication and is intentionally lengthy so the frontend can be checked for multi-line wrapping, accordion expansion, spacing, clipping, overlap, and responsive behavior.");

