	data14.put("Section 4 Group Description", "This section provides detailed patient-facing guidance regarding portal search navigation and feature availability, including expected portal behavior, common workflow questions, unusual status changes, validation scenarios, support escalation, and responsive presentation. The text is intentionally long so QA can verify wrapping, section-card expansion, spacing, scrolling, accordion behavior, mobile rendering, icon alignment, container boundaries, and overall frontend stability with larger-than-normal FAQ content.");
	data14.put("Section 4 Question Count", "11");
	data14.put("Section 4 Question 1", "What should I do if the information, status, control, or expected action related to portal search navigation and feature availability does not appear correctly in the patient portal even after I carefully review the page and wait for normal processing to finish?");
	data14.put("Section 4 Answer 1", "Review the complete information shown in the relevant portal area and confirm that you are using the correct patient record, treatment, appointment, prescription, order, laboratory activity, or account information. Allow normal processing time and verify that no required step was missed. If the expected information remains unavailable, avoid repeated submissions and contact authorized support. This guidance applies specifically to portal search navigation and feature availability and is intentionally lengthy so the frontend can be checked for multi-line wrapping, accordion expansion, spacing, clipping, overlap, and responsive behavior.");
	data14.put("Section 4 Question 2", "Why might the details shown for portal search navigation and feature availability become different from information I previously viewed in the portal, received through a notification, or discussed with the healthcare organization during an earlier interaction?");
	data14.put("Section 4 Answer 2", "The displayed information can change after updates from providers, administrators, pharmacies, laboratories, payment systems, fulfillment services, or other connected workflows. Compare the latest portal status with recent notifications or messages. If the difference could affect treatment, payment, scheduling, delivery, or another important decision, contact the appropriate healthcare team before proceeding. This guidance applies specifically to portal search navigation and feature availability and is intentionally lengthy so the frontend can be checked for multi-line wrapping, accordion expansion, spacing, clipping, overlap, and responsive behavior.");
	data14.put("Section 4 Question 3", "How can I confirm that an important action involving portal search navigation and feature availability was actually submitted and saved successfully when the page changes slowly or the final confirmation message is not immediately visible?");
	data14.put("Section 4 Answer 3", "Look for a success message, updated status, newly created record, changed value, or another visible confirmation. If the final result is unclear, review the associated history before trying again because the original request may already have succeeded. Repeating the action without checking can create duplicate orders, appointments, payments, refill requests, or other records. This guidance applies specifically to portal search navigation and feature availability and is intentionally lengthy so the frontend can be checked for multi-line wrapping, accordion expansion, spacing, clipping, overlap, and responsive behavior.");
	data14.put("Section 4 Question 4", "What should I verify before repeating an action related to portal search navigation and feature availability when the patient portal appears slow, partially loaded, temporarily unresponsive, or unable to display the expected result?");
	data14.put("Section 4 Answer 4", "Before repeating the action, confirm that the first attempt did not already create the expected result. Review the latest status, history, confirmation messages, and related patient information. Refresh only when appropriate and allow normal processing time. If the outcome remains uncertain, contact support instead of repeatedly clicking a control while the application may still be processing. This guidance applies specifically to portal search navigation and feature availability and is intentionally lengthy so the frontend can be checked for multi-line wrapping, accordion expansion, spacing, clipping, overlap, and responsive behavior.");
	data14.put("Section 4 Question 5", "What should I do if information connected with portal search navigation and feature availability appears incomplete, duplicated, outdated, inconsistent, or unexpectedly different from what I believe should currently be associated with my patient account?");
	data14.put("Section 4 Answer 5", "Compare identifiers, dates, statuses, treatment or product details, provider information, payment amounts, order information, and other visible context. Do not assume that duplicated or inconsistent records are harmless. If the difference cannot be explained from the portal, contact the healthcare organization so an authorized user can determine whether the data is current, historical, intentionally separate, or incorrect. This guidance applies specifically to portal search navigation and feature availability and is intentionally lengthy so the frontend can be checked for multi-line wrapping, accordion expansion, spacing, clipping, overlap, and responsive behavior.");
	data14.put("Section 4 Question 6", "Why might a feature, button, field, status, or other option related to portal search navigation and feature availability be available in one situation but unavailable in another even though I can still access the patient portal normally?");
	data14.put("Section 4 Answer 6", "Feature availability can depend on organization configuration, account permissions, patient eligibility, treatment state, prescription validity, product rules, provider decisions, geographic availability, billing status, laboratory requirements, or another workflow condition. If an expected option is missing, support can determine whether the behavior is intentional or caused by a portal configuration or application issue. This guidance applies specifically to portal search navigation and feature availability and is intentionally lengthy so the frontend can be checked for multi-line wrapping, accordion expansion, spacing, clipping, overlap, and responsive behavior.");
	data14.put("Section 4 Question 7", "How should portal search navigation and feature availability information behave when I open the patient portal on a mobile phone or tablet where the screen is narrower and long text must wrap across several lines without breaking the interface?");
	data14.put("Section 4 Answer 7", "On a smaller screen, long headings, descriptions, questions, and answers should wrap naturally inside their containers. Text should not overlap icons or buttons, extend outside cards, create unintended horizontal scrolling, or become clipped. Cards should expand vertically as needed and all interactive controls should remain reachable and usable on supported mobile and tablet layouts. This guidance applies specifically to portal search navigation and feature availability and is intentionally lengthy so the frontend can be checked for multi-line wrapping, accordion expansion, spacing, clipping, overlap, and responsive behavior.");
	data14.put("Section 4 Question 8", "What should I do if an unexpected error message, warning, validation message, loading indicator, or technical problem prevents me from completing an action involving portal search navigation and feature availability?");
	data14.put("Section 4 Answer 8", "Read the complete error or warning and review required fields, statuses, and instructions before trying again. If the issue appears technical, note the page, action performed, message, device, browser, and approximate time. Avoid repeated submissions when the action could create duplicate healthcare, payment, appointment, treatment, or ordering records, and contact support if the problem persists. This guidance applies specifically to portal search navigation and feature availability and is intentionally lengthy so the frontend can be checked for multi-line wrapping, accordion expansion, spacing, clipping, overlap, and responsive behavior.");
	data14.put("Section 4 Question 9", "What information should I review and prepare before contacting patient support or the healthcare team about a problem involving portal search navigation and feature availability so the issue can be investigated without unnecessary repeated actions?");
